    "lawCode": "Amd §§9-102, 9-106, 9-110, 9-112, 9-114 & 9-124, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S2346\n\nSPONSOR: KAVANAGH\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to establishing the\n\"Uniform Election Night Procedure Act\"\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill improves uniformity and clarity in article nine of the\nelection law following the enactment of the \"Election Night Poll Site\nProcedures Act of 2013\", streamlining the process for winding down poll\nsites at the end of an Election Day.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill sets forth the short title as the \"Uniform\nElection Night Procedure Act\".\n\nSection 2 of the bill amends section 9-102 of the election law, as\namended by chapter 334 of the laws of 2013, by merging and conforming\nsubsection 1 and subsection 1-a, which currently apply outside New York\nCity and within the city respectively. The procedures themselves are\nalso updated to include the use of a ballot scanner and clarifies that\nthe content of the results tape produced by such scanners may be posted\nor announced or both.\n\nSection 3 of the bill amends section 9-106 of the election, as amended\nby chapter 334 of the laws of 2013, by eliminating a reference to the\ndistinct procedures for New York City that is no longer applicable\nbecause of the amendment in section 2, above. The procedures themselves\nare also updated to require recording of seal numbers on ballot recon-\nciliation forms by poll clerks and/or inspectors.\n\nSection 4 of the bill amends section 9-110 of the election law, as\namended by chapter 334 of the laws of 2013, by removing the reference to\nsubsection 1-a, which is no longer applicable because of the amendment\nin section 2 of the bill.\n\nSection 5 of the bill amends subdivision 2 of section 9-112 of the\nelection law, as amended by chapter 334 of the laws of 2013, by removing\nthe language that permits a vote to be counted if the voter makes a hole\npunch.\n\nSection 6 of the bill amends subdivision 1 of section 9-114 of the\nelection law, as amended by chapter 334 of the laws of 2013, by empower-\ning election inspectors, in addition to poll site chairs as provided\nunder existing law, to officially record any objection to a ballot\ncounting.\n\nSection 7 of the bill amends section 9-124 of the election law, as\namended by chapter 334 of the laws of 2013, by updating the return of\ncanvass procedures and removing the sections specific to the City of New\nYork, thus setting uniform procedure throughout the State.\n\nSection 8 of the bill sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\nThis bill improves uniformity and clarity in article nine of the\nelection law following the enactment of the \"Election Night Poll Site\nProcedures Act of 2013,\" streamlining and modernizing the process for\nwinding down poll sites at the end of an Election Day to better maintain\nintegrity in the process by ensuring an orderly poll closing procedure.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPACT ON THE STATE:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPACT ON LOCALITIES:\n\nNone.\n\n \nIMPACT ON REGULATION OF BUSINESSES AND INDIVIDUALS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nIMPACT ON FINES, IMPRISONMENT, FORFEITURE OF RIGHTS, OR OTHER PENAL\nSANCTIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2018: S7090/A9606 - REFERRED TO ELECTIONS/ passed assembly\n2017: A2092 - REFERRED TO ELECTIONS/ passed assembly\n2016: S5699/A7925 - REFERRED TO ELECTIONS/ passed assembly\n2015: A7925 - REFERRED TO ELECTIONS/ passed assembly\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
